sformed classical science.","1/4|1948|events|Burma becomes independent|Burma, now Myanmar, became independent from the United Kingdom.","1/4|1958|events|Sputnik 1 re-enters atmosphere|The first artificial satellite completed its mission and burned up on re-entry.","1/5|1895|events|Dreyfus affair begins|French army officer Alfred Dreyfus was publicly stripped of rank after a conviction that became a major miscarriage-of-justice scandal.","1/5|1933|events|Golden Gate Bridge construction begins|Construction began on the landmark suspension bridge in San Francisco.","1/5|1932|births|Umberto Eco|Italian novelist, philosopher and semiotician, author of The Name of the Rose.","1/6|1838|events|Morse demonstrates telegraph|Samuel Morse demonstrated an early version of his electric telegraph.","1/6|1912|events|New Mexico becomes a state|New Mexico became the 47th state of the United States.","1/6|1412|births|Joan of Arc|French heroine who became a central figure in the Hundred Years' War.","1/7|1610|events|Galileo observes Jupiter's moons|Galileo Galilei recorded observations of three of Jupiter's moons, later identifying a fourth.","1/7|1927|events|First transatlantic telephone call|A telephone service opened between New York and London.","1/7|1943|deaths|Nikola Tesla|Serbian-American inventor and electrical engineer died in New York.","1/8|1815|events|Battle of New Orleans|Andrew Jackson's forces defeated the British after the Treaty of Ghent had been signed but before news arrived.","1/8|1959|events|Charles de Gaulle inaugurated|Charles de Gaulle became the first president of France's Fifth Republic.","1/8|1935|births|Elvis Presley|American singer and actor widely known as the King of Rock and Roll.","1/9|1793|events|First manned balloon flight in America|Jean-Pierre Blanchard made an early manned balloon ascent in the United States.","1/9|2007|events|First iPhone announced|Apple introduced its first iPhone at the Macworld conference in San Francisco.","1/9|1922|births|Har