Queen of England at Westminster Abbey.","1/15|2001|events|Wikipedia launched|The free online encyclopedia Wikipedia was launched.","1/15|1929|births|Martin Luther King Jr.|American civil-rights leader who advocated nonviolent resistance.","1/16|1547|events|Ivan IV crowned tsar|Ivan IV was crowned the first Tsar of all the Russias.","1/16|1920|events|Prohibition begins in the United States|The Eighteenth Amendment took effect, beginning national alcohol prohibition.","1/16|1932|births|Dian Fossey|American primatologist known for her long-term study of mountain gorillas.","1/17|1773|events|Cook crosses Antarctic Circle|James Cook's expedition became the first recorded ship to cross the Antarctic Circle.","1/17|1893|events|Overthrow of the Hawaiian Kingdom|Queen Liliʻuokalani was deposed in a coup backed by local and foreign interests.","1/17|1942|births|Muhammad Ali|American heavyweight boxer and global cultural figure.","1/18|1778|events|Cook reaches Hawaii|James Cook's expedition made the first recorded European landing in the Hawaiian Islands.","1/18|1919|events|Paris Peace Conference opens|Allied leaders convened to negotiate peace treaties after World War I.","1/18|1689|births|Montesquieu|French political philosopher whose ideas influenced modern constitutional government.","1/19|1809|births|Edgar Allan Poe|American writer and poet known for tales of mystery and macabre.","1/19|1915|events|First aerial bombing of Britain|German airships raided Great Yarmouth and King's Lynn during World War I.","1/19|1966|events|Indira Gandhi becomes prime minister|Indira Gandhi became India's first woman prime minister.","1/20|1265|events|First English Parliament with elected representatives|The parliament summoned by Simon de Montfort met in Westminster.","1/20|1936|events|Edward VIII becomes king|Edward VIII succeeded George V to the British throne.","1/20|1961|events|John F. Kennedy inaugurated|John F. Kennedy became the 35th president of the United States.","1/21|1793|events